A generic function asserts an interface literal whose one method is variadic in the
function's type parameter, in a package that converts a defined type to an
interface. No reading of the package states a type parameter, so the assertion keeps
the interface it writes, and every declaration here is live.

-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- go.mod --
module example.com/m

go 1.27
-- main.go --
package main

import "fmt"

// shaper is what square is used as.
type shaper interface{ Area() int }

// square is the shape main converts.
type square struct{}

// Area makes square a shaper.
func (square) Area() int { return 4 }

// mixes asserts a method variadic in T.
func mixes[T any](x any) bool {
	_, ok := x.(interface{ M(v ...T) })
	return ok
}

func main() {
	var s shaper = square{}
	fmt.Println(s.Area(), mixes[int](s))
}
